    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Trump Selection**: The caller chooses a card from their first 5 and places it face-down. This suit is the 'Hidden Rung'. 2. **Leading**: The caller leads the first trick. 3. **Following**: Players must follow suit if possible. 4. **Revealing Trump**: If a player cannot follow suit, they may ask the caller to reveal the trump. The caller turns the hidden card face-up. 5. **Winning Tricks**: Before the reveal, the highest card of the suit led wins. After the reveal, the highest trump wins (or highest cards of suit led if no trumps played).",
    Player: "1. **Trump Selection**: The caller chooses a card from their first 5 and places it face-down. This suit is the 'Hidden Rung'. 2. **Leading**: The caller leads the first trick. 3. **Following**: Players must follow suit if possible. 4. **Revealing Trump**: If a player cannot follow suit, they may ask the caller to reveal the trump. The caller turns the hidden card face-up. 5. **Winning Tricks**: Before the reveal, the highest card of the suit led wins. After the reveal, the highest trump wins (or highest cards of suit led if no trumps played).",
    objective: 'A partnership aims to win the majority (at least 7) of the 13 tricks. Special bonuses (Courts) are awarded for winning 7 consecutive tricks or 7 tricks led by the same team.',
    gameplay: "1. **Trump Selection**: The caller chooses a card from their first 5 and places it face-down. This suit is the 'Hidden Rung'. 2. **Leading**: The caller leads the first trick. 3. **Following**: Players must follow suit if possible. 4. **Revealing Trump**: If a player cannot follow suit, they may ask the caller to reveal the trump. The caller turns the hidden card face-up. 5. **Winning Tricks**: Before the reveal, the highest card of the suit led wins. After the reveal, the highest trump wins (or highest cards of suit led if no trumps played).",
    keyRules: [
      'Trumps cannot be played to a trick until they have been revealed.',
      'Once revealed, a player void in the led suit MUST play a trump if they have one.',
      'The hidden trump card itself can be used to win a trick once revealed.',
      "If a team wins the first 7 tricks consecutively, it is a 'Court' (instant game win).",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in fixed partnerships (North-South vs. East-West).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces are high (A-K-Q-J-10...2).',
      equipment: "52-card deck and a way to track tricks (or 'Courts').",
      dealing: "The dealer deals 5 cards to each player in the first batch. The player to the dealer's right (Trump Caller) selects their hidden trump. The remaining cards are then dealt in batches of 4 until all cards are distributed (13 per player).",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Trump Selection**: The caller chooses a card from their first 5 and places it face-down. This suit is the 'Hidden Rung'. 2. **Leading**: The caller leads the first trick. 3. **Following**: Players must follow suit if possible. 4. **Revealing Trump**: If a player cannot follow suit, they may ask the caller to reveal the trump. The caller turns the hidden card face-up. 5. **Winning Tricks**: Before the reveal, the highest card of the suit led wins. After the reveal, the highest trump wins (or highest cards of suit led if no trumps played).",
